From: SM-A105F Linux 6.18.54 board port
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: exynos: describe Exynos7885 removable SD host

Describe the disabled second DesignWare MMC host at the community-reported
A10 Exynos7885 address/IRQ, using upstream clock handles and current binding
shape. The legacy four-cell Samsung timing tuples are converted to upstream
(sample, drive) two-cell tuples: legacy fields are divider, fine-drive,
drive, sample. The divider is represented separately as required upstream.

The host stays disabled because exact Samsung-source confirmation, board
pinctrl, card detect, supplies, and physical validation are still pending.
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos7885.dtsi | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos7885.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos7885.dtsi
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos7885.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos7885.dtsi
@@ -310,6 +310,22 @@
 			status = "disabled";
 		};

+		/* Optional removable SD host; board DTS supplies pins and slot details. */
+		mmc_2: mmc@13550000 {
+			compatible = "samsung,exynos7-dw-mshc";
+			reg = <0x13550000 0x2000>;
+			interrupts = <GIC_SPI 147 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
+			#address-cells = <1>;
+			#size-cells = <0>;
+			clocks = <&cmu_fsys CLK_GOUT_MMC_CARD_ACLK>,
+				 <&cmu_fsys CLK_GOUT_MMC_CARD_SDCLKIN>;
+			clock-names = "biu", "ciu";
+			fifo-depth = <0x40>;
+			samsung,dw-mshc-ciu-div = <3>;
+			samsung,dw-mshc-sdr-timing = <0 2>;
+			samsung,dw-mshc-ddr-timing = <1 2>;
+			status = "disabled";
+		};

 		serial_0: serial@13800000 {
